<title>UK: GECC sets $300 million three-year Eurobond.</title>
<headline>GECC sets $300 million three-year Eurobond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond was announced by lead manager SBC Warburg.</p>
<p> BORROWER   GENERAL ELECTRIC CAPITAL CORP</p>
<p> AMT	  $300 MLN  COUPON     6.25	MATURITY    26.JUN.00</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE  100.7235  PAY DATE    26.JUN.97</p>
<p> FULL FEES  1.375     REOFFER    99.536    SPREAD	-3 BP</p>
<p> S&amp;P	  AAA	 DENOMS (K) 1-10-100  SALE LIMITS US/GB</p>
<p> NEG PLG    NO	  CRS DEFLT  YES	 FORCE MAJ   YES</p>
<p> GOV LAW    =	   HOME CTRY  U.S.	TAX PROVS   STANDARD</p>
<p> MGT/UND    0.1875    SELL CONC  1.1875    PRAECIPUUM  NONE</p>
<p>UNDERLYING GOVT BOND 6.375 PCTU.S. T-NOTE DUE 15.MAY.00</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
</text>
